---
// Case D — Indonesia in the Global Narrative. Page anatomy per spec N5:
// pulse hero → eras → tone → themes → who's talking → event layer → methodology.
// Identity: signal violet on broadcast black. Every chart is d3 (SVG / canvas-2D);
// no WebGL anywhere — the user's browser has it disabled.
import "../styles/tokens.css";
const summary = (await import("../data/summary.json").catch(() => null))?.default ?? {};
const fmtPct = (v) => (v == null ? "—" : (v * 1).toFixed(2) + "%");
const apiLast = summary.apiLast ?? "—";
const eventsLast = summary.eventsLast ?? "pending";
// The share has two halves. After the review of this case, the page states both
// wherever it would otherwise invite a reader to hear "attention" and think "the world".
const chg = (v) => (v == null ? "—" : `${v > 0 ? "+" : "−"}${Math.abs(v * 100).toFixed(0)}%`);
const nInt = (v) => (v == null ? "—" : Math.round(v).toLocaleString("en-US"));
// The review's own numbers, read from the same file the review article draws on, so
// the two pages can never disagree. (pipeline/article.py writes it.)
const rv = (await import("../data/article.json").catch(() => null))?.default ?? null;
const flipped = rv
  ? rv.attr.anchor_foreign.filter((a) => (a.published_api_ratio >= 1.5) !== (a.foreign.ratio >= 1.5)).length
  : null;
---
<html lang="en" data-case="narrative" data-theme="dark">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Indonesia in the Global Narrative</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Archivo:wght@500;600;700&family=Public+Sans:wght@400;500;600&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="stamp-bar">
      <span class="stamp">INDONESIA IN THE GLOBAL NARRATIVE</span>
      <span class="stamp dim" id="vintage">GDELT · API THROUGH {apiLast} · EVENTS THROUGH {eventsLast}</span>
    </header>

    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-top">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <span class="eyebrow">GDELT open feeds · 2017 → now</span>
          <h1>Every time the world’s news turned to Indonesia — a decade, one pulse.</h1>
          <p>GDELT machine-reads the world’s news every fifteen minutes in 65 languages. This is the share of
          all of it that mentioned Indonesia, day by day{summary.volMean ? ` — on average ${fmtPct(summary.volMean)} of everything monitored` : ""}.
          The flares are the days Indonesia took an unusually large slice of the world’s coverage — which
          happens both when Indonesia is covered more and when everything else is covered less. Our review
          found that most of the biggest spikes are partly the second; read the marked days as
          <em>events worth looking up</em>, not as a ranking of how much the world cared.</p>
        </div>
        <aside class="hero-figures" id="hero-figures" aria-label="Headline figures for the attention pulse">
          <div class="figs-pending" id="hero-status">
            <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="stamp dim">READING THE PULSE…</span>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </div>
      <div id="pulse" class="pulse"></div>
      <ol id="anchor-key" class="anchor-key" hidden></ol>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter wide">
      <span class="eyebrow">01 · The eras</span>
      <h2>Five regimes of coverage</h2>
      <p>Each era below carries its average share of world coverage, its mean tone, and the themes that
      defined it — all computed, none asserted. Read the share against the two numbers underneath it.
      Between {summary.firstYear ?? "—"} and {summary.lastYear ?? "—"} the articles GDELT saw naming
      Indonesia fell {chg(summary.idnChange)} — from {nInt(summary.idnFirst)} a day to
      {nInt(summary.idnLast)} — while everything it monitored fell {chg(summary.monitoredChange)}.
      The share rose {chg(summary.shareChange)} because the second fell faster than the first.
      <b>These are five regimes of what Indonesia’s slice looked like, not five regimes of how much the
      world was watching</b> — a distinction the review article takes apart in detail.</p>
      <div id="eras" class="era-grid"></div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter">
      <span class="eyebrow">02 · The darkest days</span>
      <h2>How warmly the world spoke</h2>
      <p>GDELT’s tone runs from roughly −10 (uniformly negative) to +10. Coverage of any country lives
      below zero — news is what goes wrong — so the line is drawn against its own long-run mean: teal
      when the world was kinder than usual to Indonesia, coral when it was harsher.</p>
      <div id="tone-chart" class="chart"></div>
      <div id="darkest" class="day-list"></div>
      <p class="footnote" id="g20-note"></p>
      <h3>When it’s loud, is it dark?</h3>
      <p class="footnote">Each dot is a month: how much the world talked about Indonesia against how it
      sounded. At this resolution the two barely correlate (the r is on the chart) — sustained attention
      comes from summits and elections as often as from catastrophe. <b>But the answer depends on the
      timescale, and this is the one scale at which it vanishes.</b> Measured day by day the correlation is
      negative, and the loudest tenth of days is about a fifth of a tone point darker than the rest: loud
      days are dark, loud months are not. The review article shows both. Notice also the colour drift:
      months after 2023 sit warmer — the review decomposes that rise and finds roughly two-thirds is the
      same outlets writing more warmly and one-third is GDELT reading a different set of outlets.</p>
      <div id="scatter" class="chart"></div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter wide">
      <span class="eyebrow">03 · What the world reads about</span>
      <h2>The threads in the story</h2>
      <p>Each panel is a keyword theme’s share of all Indonesia coverage, month by month, on its own
      scale. Because both halves of that ratio share the same denominator, this is the one layer on the
      page the crawl’s size cannot move. Hover to read one month across every theme.</p>
      <p class="footnote">Twenty theme queries were registered; the ones below are those the rate-limited
      API has returned so far, and each panel states how many months it holds. A panel with a short window
      is <b>not</b> comparable with a full one — its mean is a mean of those months only.</p>
      <div id="themes" class="theme-grid"></div>
      <div id="era-rank" class="rank-wrap"></div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter wide">
      <span class="eyebrow">04 · Who’s talking</span>
      <h2>Whose news it is</h2>
      <p>For each publishing country, the share of its <em>own</em> monitored output that mentioned
      Indonesia — a measure of interest, not of volume. Neighbours watch closely; the Anglophone giants
      barely glance, and when they do the tone is different.</p>
      <p class="footnote">Two cautions on this chapter. The intensity below is <b>not size-controlled</b>:
      a country GDELT barely indexes can float to the top on a handful of articles, so read the large
      neighbours and ignore the tail. And this measure cannot tell you who supplies the bulk of the
      coverage. Counting publishers directly in the event layer — which the review article does — shows
      that {summary.translatedShare ? `${Math.round(summary.translatedShare * 100)}%` : "most"} of the
      kept events come from the translated feed and that the great majority of all Indonesia coverage
      here is published in Indonesia. This is substantially Indonesia’s own press, not the world’s.</p>
      <div id="sources-heat" class="chart"></div>
      <div class="two-up">
        <div><h3>Foreign vs domestic press</h3><p class="footnote">Share of Indonesia coverage published outside Indonesia (<code>-sourcecountry:ID</code>). This is the query the API refuses most often, so the curve is still pending; the review article builds the same split from the event layer instead, and finds foreign-published coverage of Indonesia <em>falling</em> across the decade while the share above rises.</p><div id="press-chart" class="chart"></div></div>
        <div><h3>Languages</h3><p class="footnote">Intensity of Indonesia coverage by language — the world’s narrative is not only the English one.</p><div id="lang-bars" class="chart"></div></div>
      </div>
      <div id="outlets" class="two-up"></div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter wide">
      <span class="eyebrow">05 · The event layer</span>
      <h2>What actually happened, and where</h2>
      <p>Underneath the articles, GDELT codes discrete events — who did what to whom, where. From the raw
      15-minute feed we keep every event that touches Indonesia (as location or as actor), count it
      against everything the feed carried that day, and type it: cooperation or conflict, words or deeds.</p>
      <div id="events-status" class="stamp dim"></div>
      <h3>Cooperation and conflict, month by month</h3>
      <div id="quad-chart" class="chart"></div>
      <h3>Protest events</h3>
      <p class="footnote">CAMEO root code 14. The 2019 post-election riots and the 2025 protests are the two
      spikes the pipeline must reproduce unprompted — the anchor-event check.</p>
      <div id="protest-chart" class="chart"></div>
      <h3>Where the news happened</h3>
      <p class="footnote">Event locations on a 0.25° grid; the archipelago draws itself from the data — no
      basemap. Events geocoded only to “Indonesia” (no province) are excluded and counted below.</p>
      <div class="map-controls">
        <div class="toggle" role="group" aria-label="colour by" id="map-mode">
          <button data-mode="n" class="on">EVENTS</button><button data-mode="tone">TONE</button><button data-mode="protest">PROTESTS</button>
        </div>
        <div class="toggle" id="map-years" role="group" aria-label="year"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="map-wrap"><canvas id="map-canvas"></canvas><div id="map-tip" hidden></div><span class="stamp dim map-note" id="map-note"></span></div>
      <div class="two-up">
        <div><h3>Who Indonesia is in the news with</h3><p class="footnote">Counter-party actors in Indonesia events — CAMEO codes: ISO3 countries plus regions (SEA = Southeast Asia). All years streamed so far.</p><div id="actors" class="chart"></div></div>
        <div><h3>Event types</h3><p class="footnote">CAMEO root codes across all kept events.</p><div id="roots" class="chart"></div></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter review-cta">
      <span class="eyebrow">06 · Review</span>
      <h2>Audited adversarially, by its own author.</h2>
      <p>A second read of the same archive against the published literature, written to attack the first. It was done by the person who built the instrument — no external reviewer has checked it, and one person reviews everything here — if you would like to be the first, breaking a gate here is worth more than another instrument. It finds that
      {rv ? `${Math.round(rv.crawl.elasticity.attributable * 100)}%` : "most"} of the decade’s apparent
      rise in attention is predicted by GDELT’s shrinking crawl; that {rv ? rv.spikes.weekend_mon : "24"}
      of the {rv ? rv.spikes.n_top : "30"} loudest days fall on a Saturday, Sunday or Monday, when the
      world’s newsroom is quiet; that {rv ? rv.attr.publishers.indonesian_in_top25 : "23"} of the
      {rv ? rv.attr.publishers.top.length : "25"} largest publishers here are based in Indonesia; and it
      rebuilds the anchor test on foreign publishers only, which changes {flipped ?? "five"} of
      {rv ? rv.attr.anchor_foreign.length : "nine"} verdicts. The corrections it asked for have been
      applied to this page.</p>
      <a class="cta big" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "")}/article`}>Read the review article →</a>
    </section>

    <footer class="method">
      <span class="eyebrow">Methodology &amp; sources</span>
      <h3>Normalization, and what it cannot fix</h3>
      <p>GDELT’s crawl is not a constant: the number of articles it monitors per day has drifted by a factor
      of about {summary.crawlDrift ?? "four"} across the decade — mostly <em>shrinking</em> since
      {summary.firstYear ?? 2017}. Every attention chart on this page is therefore a <b>share</b> of
      everything monitored, never a raw count, which is what the API's own documentation recommends and
      what keeps one day comparable with the next.</p>
      <p><b>It does not make one decade comparable with another, and this page used to imply it did.</b>
      Over the window the raw count fell {chg(summary.idnChange)} and the crawl fell
      {chg(summary.monitoredChange)}, so the share rose {chg(summary.shareChange)}. Our review estimates
      that {rv ? `${Math.round(rv.crawl.elasticity.attributable * 100)}%` : "most"} of that rise is
      predicted by the crawl’s shrinkage alone, and that counting only
      publishers outside Indonesia gives a series moving the other way. Neither the raw count nor the
      share identifies the world’s interest on its own; both are plotted here so the gap is visible.
      (The API itself went dark 15 Jun – 1 Jul 2025; that gap is left visible, not interpolated.)</p>
      <div id="norm-chart" class="chart"></div>
      <h3>Sources, coding, cadence</h3>
      <p class="muted"><b>Data source and terms.</b> All figures on this page derive from
      <a href="https://www.gdeltproject.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The GDELT
      Project</a> — the DOC 2.0 API and the raw 15-minute <code>export</code> feed — used
      under GDELT's own published terms of use, which permit unrestricted use with
      attribution. Nothing here redistributes GDELT's data: the pipeline fetches it, and only
      derived counts are published. Base maps and administrative boundaries carry their own
      licences, stated with each layer.</p>
      <p id="method-text">Curves: GDELT DOC 2.0 API (<code>TimelineVol</code>, pre-normalized;
      <code>TimelineVolRaw</code> with its <code>norm</code>; <code>TimelineTone</code>;
      <code>TimelineSourceCountry</code>; <code>TimelineLang</code>), keyless, one request per ~12 s, every
      response cached. Events: the raw 15-minute <code>export</code> feed (English + translated), 2017 → now,
      ~50 GB streamed through a filter that keeps rows where <code>ActionGeo_CountryCode = 'ID'</code> — that is
      the <b>FIPS</b> code — or <code>Actor1/2CountryCode = 'IDN'</code> — the <b>ISO3</b> code. The two column
      families use different standards; matching only one silently drops a third of Indonesia’s events.
      Events are counted once each (GDELT’s export is one row per unique event; mentions are kept only as
      weights). The ledger keys on <code>DATEADDED</code>, the day the news carried the event, because GDELT’s
      guessed event date mis-years undated references. <code>sourcecountry:</code> is the publisher’s country,
      not the story’s. Tone and event types are machine-coded; counts are indicative. Media coverage is
      itself biased — toward disaster, toward the Anglophone press, toward what is online — and this page
      measures that coverage, not Indonesia.</p>
      <h3>Validation gates</h3>
      <div id="gates" class="gates" data-flipped={flipped == null ? "" : String(flipped)}></div>
      <p class="footnote">Data: <a href="https://www.gdeltproject.org/" rel="noopener">The GDELT Project</a> — free for any use
      with attribution. A demo-lab case; refreshed nightly (API) and by month (events).</p>
      <span class="stamp dim" id="foot-stamp"></span>
    </footer>
    <div id="chart-tip" hidden></div>

    <script>
      import * as d3 from "d3";

      /* visible failure beats silent emptiness: any uncaught error paints a banner */
      const failBanner = (msg) => {
        let b = document.getElementById("err-banner");
        if (!b) {
          b = document.createElement("div"); b.id = "err-banner";
          b.style.cssText = "position:fixed;bottom:0;left:0;right:0;z-index:99;background:#3A1E1A;color:#F26D5B;font:12px ui-monospace,monospace;padding:10px 16px;border-top:1px solid #F26D5B;";
          document.body.appendChild(b);
        }
        b.textContent = "⚠ " + msg;
      };
      addEventListener("error", (e) => failBanner("Script error: " + (e.message ?? e.type)));
      addEventListener("unhandledrejection", (e) => failBanner("Load error: " + (e.reason?.message ?? e.reason)));
      /* run each section independently — one failure must not blank the page */
      const sect = (name, fn) => { try { return fn(); } catch (err) { console.error(name, err); failBanner(`${name} failed: ${err.message ?? err}`); return null; } };

      const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
      const VIOLET = "#B26DF2", POS = "#4BB8A9", NEG = "#F26D5B", INK = "#EAE6F2", MUTED = "#9C93B3", GROUND = "#0E0A16", HAIR = "#2A2142", SURFACE = "#171126";
      const ERA_COLORS = ["#7A6FA8", "#B26DF2", "#4BB8A9", "#E0A63F", "#F26D5B"];
      const reduced = matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches;
      const load = (f) => fetch(`${base}/data/${f}`).then((r) => { if (!r.ok) throw new Error(f); return r.json(); });
      const get = (f) => load(f).catch(() => null);
      const [pulse, tone, themes, sources, events, map, status] = await Promise.all(
        ["pulse.json", "tone.json", "themes.json", "sources.json", "events.json", "map.json", "status.json"].map(get));

      const pending = (id, msg) => { const el = document.getElementById(id); if (el) el.innerHTML = `<div class="pending">${msg}</div>`; };
      if (!pulse) {
        document.getElementById("hero-status").innerHTML =
          `<span class="stamp dim">PIPELINE STILL RUNNING — the API curves have not been exported yet. Refresh in a few minutes.</span>`;
      }
      if (status) {
        const v = document.getElementById("vintage");
        v.textContent = `GDELT · API THROUGH ${status.api_last ?? "—"} · EVENTS ${status.events_complete ? "THROUGH" : "PARTIAL, THROUGH"} ${status.events_last ?? "PENDING"}`;
        document.getElementById("foot-stamp").textContent =
          `AN OPENSTUDY.ID INSTRUMENT · GENERATED ${status.generated ?? ""} · ${status.api_timelines ?? 0} API TIMELINES · ${status.streamed?.files?.toLocaleString() ?? 0} FEED FILES / ${status.streamed?.gb ?? 0} GB STREAMED · ${status.streamed?.rows_kept?.toLocaleString() ?? 0} INDONESIA EVENTS KEPT`;
      }

      /* shared helpers */
      const ctip = document.getElementById("chart-tip");
      const showTip = (e, html) => { ctip.hidden = false; ctip.innerHTML = html; const x = Math.min(e.pageX + 14, innerWidth + scrollX - 280); ctip.style.left = x + "px"; ctip.style.top = e.pageY + 14 + "px"; };
      const hideTip = () => { ctip.hidden = true; };
      const P = d3.timeParse("%Y-%m-%d"), PM = d3.timeParse("%Y-%m");
      const fDay = d3.timeFormat("%-d %b %Y"), fMon = d3.timeFormat("%b %Y"), fYear = d3.timeFormat("%Y");
      const pct = (v, d = 2) => (v == null ? "—" : v.toFixed(d) + "%");
      const num = (v, d = 2) => (v == null ? "—" : (+v).toFixed(d));
      const sgn = (v, d = 2) => (v == null || Number.isNaN(+v) ? "—" : (v > 0 ? "+" : "") + (+v).toFixed(d));
      const mkSvg = (el, H) => { const W = el.clientWidth || 800; const svg = d3.select(el).append("svg").attr("width", W).attr("height", H).attr("viewBox", `0 0 ${W} ${H}`); return { svg, W, H }; };
      /* A descriptive legend is a caption, not a datum: rendered in the flow it wraps to the
         container instead of clipping against the plot edge on a narrow screen. */
      const capNote = (el, html) => el.insertAdjacentHTML("beforebegin", `<p class="chart-note">${html}</p>`);
      const swatch = (c, label) => `<span class="sw"><i style="background:${c}"></i>${label}</span>`;
      const yearAxis = (x) => d3.axisBottom(x).ticks(d3.timeYear.every(1)).tickFormat(fYear).tickSizeOuter(0);
      const nearestIdx = (dates, t) => { const i = d3.bisector((d) => d).left(dates, t); return i <= 0 ? 0 : i >= dates.length ? dates.length - 1 : (t - dates[i - 1] < dates[i] - t ? i - 1 : i); };
      const hoverRect = (svg, M, W, H, onMove, onLeave) => svg.append("rect").attr("class", "hover").attr("x", M.l).attr("y", M.t).attr("width", Math.max(0, W - M.l - M.r)).attr("height", Math.max(0, H - M.t - M.b)).attr("fill", "transparent").on("mousemove", onMove).on("mouseleave", onLeave);
      const defs = d3.select("body").append("svg").attr("width", 0).attr("height", 0).style("position", "absolute").append("defs");
      const glow = defs.append("filter").attr("id", "violet-glow").attr("x", "-40%").attr("y", "-40%").attr("width", "180%").attr("height", "180%");
      glow.append("feDropShadow").attr("dx", 0).attr("dy", 0).attr("stdDeviation", 4).attr("flood-color", VIOLET).attr("flood-opacity", 0.55);
      const fade = defs.append("linearGradient").attr("id", "pulse-fill").attr("x1", 0).attr("y1", 0).attr("x2", 0).attr("y2", 1);
      fade.append("stop").attr("offset", "0%").attr("stop-color", VIOLET).attr("stop-opacity", 0.55);
      fade.append("stop").attr("offset", "100%").attr("stop-color", VIOLET).attr("stop-opacity", 0.02);

      /* ---------- hero: the pulse ---------- */
      sect("pulse", () => {
        if (!pulse) return;
        const el = document.getElementById("pulse");
        const dates = pulse.dates.map(P);
        const vol7 = pulse.vol7, vol = pulse.vol;
        const M = { t: 64, r: 28, b: 34, l: 40 };
        const { svg, W, H } = mkSvg(el, Math.max(340, Math.min(520, innerHeight * 0.58)));
        const x = d3.scaleTime(d3.extent(dates), [M.l, W - M.r]);
        const y = d3.scaleLinear([0, d3.max(vol.filter((v) => v != null)) * 1.04], [H - M.b, M.t]);
        // era bands — the label is drawn only where its own band can hold it, so
        // narrow viewports drop labels instead of overprinting them.
        const erasG = svg.append("g");
        const CHW = 7.4;                       // ~char width of the 12px mono annot face
        (pulse.eras ?? []).forEach((e, i) => {
          const x0 = x(P(e.start)), x1 = x(P(e.end)), bw = Math.max(0, x1 - x0);
          erasG.append("rect").attr("x", x0).attr("y", M.t - 30).attr("width", bw).attr("height", H - M.b - M.t + 30).attr("fill", ERA_COLORS[i % ERA_COLORS.length]).attr("opacity", 0.045);
          if (bw > 6) erasG.append("line").attr("x1", x0).attr("x2", x0).attr("y1", M.t - 30).attr("y2", H - M.b).attr("stroke", ERA_COLORS[i % ERA_COLORS.length]).attr("stroke-opacity", 0.3);
          const txt = e.label.toUpperCase();
          if (bw < txt.length * CHW * 1.12 + 12) return;   // no room: leave the band unlabelled
          erasG.append("text").attr("class", "annot era-band").attr("x", x0 + 8).attr("y", M.t - 15).attr("fill", ERA_COLORS[i % ERA_COLORS.length]).text(txt);
        });
        svg.append("g").attr("class", "axis").attr("transform", `translate(0,${H - M.b})`).call(yearAxis(x));
        svg.append("g").attr("class", "axis").attr("transform", `translate(${M.l},0)`).call(d3.axisLeft(y).ticks(4).tickFormat((v) => v + "%").tickSizeOuter(0));
        svg.append("text").attr("class", "annot").attr("x", M.l + 6).attr("y", M.t + 8).text(W < 760 ? "share of world news, 7-day mean" : "share of all articles GDELT monitored, 7-day mean");
        const clipId = "pulse-clip";
        const clip = svg.append("clipPath").attr("id", clipId).append("rect").attr("x", M.l).attr("y", 0).attr("height", H).attr("width", reduced ? W : 0);
        const g = svg.append("g").attr("clip-path", `url(#${clipId})`);
        const area = d3.area().defined((d, i) => vol7[i] != null).x((d) => x(d)).y0(H - M.b).y1((d, i) => y(vol7[i])).curve(d3.curveMonotoneX);
        const line = d3.line().defined((d, i) => vol7[i] != null).x((d) => x(d)).y((d, i) => y(vol7[i])).curve(d3.curveMonotoneX);
        const daily = d3.line().defined((d, i) => vol[i] != null).x((d) => x(d)).y((d, i) => y(vol[i]));
        g.append("path").datum(dates).attr("d", area).attr("fill", "url(#pulse-fill)");
        g.append("path").datum(dates).attr("d", daily).attr("fill", "none").attr("stroke", VIOLET).attr("stroke-width", 0.6).attr("opacity", 0.28);
        g.append("path").datum(dates).attr("d", line).attr("fill", "none").attr("stroke", VIOLET).attr("stroke-width", 1.8).style("filter", "url(#violet-glow)");
        // anchors
        const anchors = (pulse.anchors ?? []).map((a, i) => ({ ...a, i, x: x(P(a.peak_day ?? a.day)), y: y(Math.min(a.peak ?? 0, y.domain()[1])) }));
        const ag = svg.append("g").attr("class", "anchors");
        const lab = ag.selectAll("g.a").data(anchors).join("g").attr("class", "a").attr("opacity", reduced ? 1 : 0);
        // Narrow viewports cannot hold a 300px dated caption inside the plot at a
        // legible size, so the chart carries numbered markers and the captions move
        // to an ordered key beneath it. Wide viewports keep the in-place callouts.
        const KEYED = W < 760;
        anchors.forEach((d, i) => { d.n = i + 1; d.text = `${fDay(P(d.day))} · ${d.label}`; });

        lab.append("circle").attr("cx", (d) => d.x).attr("cy", (d) => d.y).attr("r", KEYED ? 8.5 : 3.4)
          .attr("fill", (d) => (KEYED ? GROUND : d.verdict === "FAIL" ? NEG : INK))
          .attr("stroke", (d) => (KEYED ? (d.verdict === "FAIL" ? NEG : VIOLET) : GROUND)).attr("stroke-width", KEYED ? 1.4 : 1);

        if (KEYED) {
          lab.append("text").attr("class", "annot amark").attr("x", (d) => d.x).attr("y", (d) => d.y + 4)
            .attr("text-anchor", "middle").attr("fill", (d) => (d.verdict === "FAIL" ? NEG : INK)).text((d) => d.n);
          const key = document.getElementById("anchor-key");
          key.hidden = false;
          key.innerHTML = anchors.map((d) => `<li><span class="akey-n${d.verdict === "FAIL" ? " fail" : ""}">${d.n}</span><span class="akey-t"><b>${fDay(P(d.day))}</b> · ${d.label}</span></li>`).join("");
        } else {
          // In-place callouts: each caption is measured, clamped inside the plot, and
          // assigned the first stagger row whose occupied interval it clears.
          const CW = 7.4, LH = 15.5, GAP = 14;
          const inner0 = M.l + 2, inner1 = W - M.r - 2;
          anchors.forEach((d) => {
            d.w = d.text.length * CW;
            d.flip = d.x + d.w + 6 > inner1;            // hug the right edge instead of overflowing
            let x0 = d.flip ? d.x - d.w - 6 : d.x + 6;
            x0 = Math.max(inner0, Math.min(x0, inner1 - d.w));
            d.lx0 = x0; d.lx1 = x0 + d.w;
          });
          const rowEnd = [];
          [...anchors].sort((a, b) => a.lx0 - b.lx0).forEach((d) => {
            let r = 0; while (rowEnd[r] != null && d.lx0 < rowEnd[r] + GAP) r++;
            rowEnd[r] = d.lx1; d.row = r;
          });
          const labY = (d) => M.t + 26 + d.row * LH;
          // leader: down from the caption, then a jog across to the dot when clamping moved it
          lab.append("path").attr("d", (d) => {
            const ax = d.flip ? d.lx1 : d.lx0, y0 = labY(d) + 5;
            return Math.abs(ax - d.x) < 3 ? `M${d.x},${y0}V${d.y - 6}` : `M${ax},${y0}V${d.y - 12}H${d.x}V${d.y - 6}`;
          }).attr("fill", "none").attr("stroke", INK).attr("stroke-opacity", 0.28).attr("stroke-dasharray", "2 3");
          lab.append("text").attr("class", "annot alabel").attr("x", (d) => (d.flip ? d.lx1 : d.lx0)).attr("y", labY)
            .attr("fill", INK).attr("text-anchor", (d) => (d.flip ? "end" : "start")).text((d) => d.text);
        }
        const flare = (d) => { ag.append("circle").attr("cx", d.x).attr("cy", d.y).attr("r", 2).attr("fill", "none").attr("stroke", VIOLET).attr("stroke-width", 2).attr("opacity", 0.9).transition().duration(900).ease(d3.easeCubicOut).attr("r", 26).attr("opacity", 0).remove(); };
        // hover
        const guide = svg.append("line").attr("y1", M.t).attr("y2", H - M.b).attr("stroke", INK).attr("stroke-opacity", 0.5).style("display", "none");
        const dot = svg.append("circle").attr("r", 4).attr("fill", VIOLET).attr("stroke", GROUND).style("display", "none");
        hoverRect(svg, M, W, H, (e) => {
          const i = nearestIdx(dates, x.invert(d3.pointer(e)[0])); if (vol[i] == null && vol7[i] == null) return;
          guide.style("display", null).attr("x1", x(dates[i])).attr("x2", x(dates[i]));
          dot.style("display", null).attr("cx", x(dates[i])).attr("cy", y(vol7[i] ?? vol[i]));
          const near = anchors.find((a) => Math.abs(P(a.day) - dates[i]) < 4 * 864e5);
          showTip(e, `<b>${fDay(dates[i])}</b><br>share of world news <b>${pct(vol[i])}</b> · 7-day ${pct(vol7[i])}<br>tone ${sgn(pulse.tone?.[i])}${near ? `<br><span class="violet">◆ ${near.label}</span>` : ""}`);
        }, () => { guide.style("display", "none"); dot.style("display", "none"); hideTip(); });
        // The figures are known the moment the data is in hand — publish them now, so the
        // pending state never outlives the render it was standing in for.
        const fig = (k, v, sub) => `<div class="fig"><span class="stamp dim">${k}</span><b>${v}</b>${sub ? `<span class="fig-sub">${sub}</span>` : ""}</div>`;
        document.getElementById("hero-figures").innerHTML =
          fig("DAYS OBSERVED", dates.length.toLocaleString(), "2017 → now, daily") +
          fig("PEAK SHARE", pct(pulse.vol_peak), fDay(P(pulse.vol_peak_day))) +
          fig("DECADE MEAN", pct(pulse.vol_mean), "of all world news") +
          fig("ANCHOR EVENTS", String(anchors.length), "dated, pre-registered");
        if (reduced) return;
        const dur = 5200, t0 = performance.now(), fired = new Set();
        const step = (t) => {
          const k = Math.min((t - t0) / dur, 1), xe = M.l + k * (W - M.l - M.r);
          clip.attr("width", Math.max(0, xe - M.l));
          anchors.forEach((a) => { if (!fired.has(a.i) && a.x <= xe) { fired.add(a.i); flare(a); lab.filter((d) => d.i === a.i).transition().duration(500).attr("opacity", 1); } });
          if (k < 1) requestAnimationFrame(step);
        };
        requestAnimationFrame(step);
      });

      /* ---------- chapter 1: eras ---------- */
      sect("eras", () => {
        const el = document.getElementById("eras");
        if (!pulse?.eras?.length) { pending("eras", "Pipeline still running — era summaries appear once the API curves are exported."); return; }
        const maxVol = d3.max(pulse.eras, (e) => e.vol_mean);
        el.innerHTML = pulse.eras.map((e, i) => `
          <article class="era" style="--c:${ERA_COLORS[i % ERA_COLORS.length]}">
            <span class="stamp" style="color:var(--c)">${fYear(P(e.start))}${fYear(P(e.start)) !== fYear(P(e.end)) ? "–" + fYear(P(e.end)) : ""}</span>
            <h3>${e.label}</h3>
            <div class="era-stat"><span class="stamp dim">SHARE OF WORLD NEWS</span><b>${pct(e.vol_mean, 3)}</b><div class="bar"><i style="width:${(100 * e.vol_mean / maxVol).toFixed(1)}%"></i></div></div>
            ${e.idn_mean != null ? `<div class="era-row split"><div><span class="stamp dim">ARTICLES/DAY</span><b>${Math.round(e.idn_mean).toLocaleString()}</b></div>
              <div><span class="stamp dim">CRAWL/DAY</span><b>${d3.format(".2s")(e.monitored_mean)}</b></div></div>` : ""}
            <div class="era-row"><div><span class="stamp dim">TONE</span><b style="color:${e.tone_mean < (pulse.eras.reduce((s, x) => s + x.tone_mean, 0) / pulse.eras.length) ? NEG : POS}">${sgn(e.tone_mean)}</b></div>
              <div><span class="stamp dim">PEAK DAY</span><b>${fDay(P(e.peak_day))}</b></div></div>
            <div class="chips">${e.top_themes.map((t) => `<span class="chip">${t.label} <i>${pct(100 * t.share, 0)}</i></span>`).join("")}</div>
            ${e.events != null ? `<span class="stamp dim">${e.events.toLocaleString()} EVENTS · ${e.protests?.toLocaleString() ?? 0} PROTEST</span>` : `<span class="stamp dim">EVENT LAYER PENDING</span>`}
          </article>`).join("");
      });

      /* ---------- chapter 2: tone ---------- */
      sect("tone chart", () => {
        const el = document.getElementById("tone-chart");
        if (!tone?.tone?.some((v) => v != null)) { pending("tone-chart", "Pipeline still running — the tone curve is not cached yet."); pending("darkest", "Darkest-day briefs follow the tone curve."); return; }
        const dates = tone.dates.map(P), t28 = tone.tone28, t1 = tone.tone, mean = tone.mean;
        const M = { t: 18, r: 20, b: 30, l: 40 }, { svg, W, H } = mkSvg(el, 300);
        const x = d3.scaleTime(d3.extent(dates), [M.l, W - M.r]);
        const ext = d3.extent(t1.filter((v) => v != null)); const y = d3.scaleLinear([Math.min(ext[0], mean - 2), Math.max(ext[1], mean + 1.5)], [H - M.b, M.t]).nice();
        svg.append("g").attr("class", "axis").attr("transform", `translate(0,${H - M.b})`).call(yearAxis(x));
        svg.append("g").attr("class", "axis").attr("transform", `translate(${M.l},0)`).call(d3.axisLeft(y).ticks(5).tickSizeOuter(0));
        svg.append("clipPath").attr("id", "tone-above").append("rect").attr("x", 0).attr("y", 0).attr("width", W).attr("height", y(mean));
        svg.append("clipPath").attr("id", "tone-below").append("rect").attr("x", 0).attr("y", y(mean)).attr("width", W).attr("height", H - y(mean));
        const area = d3.area().defined((d, i) => t28[i] != null).x((d) => x(d)).y0(y(mean)).y1((d, i) => y(t28[i])).curve(d3.curveMonotoneX);
        svg.append("path").datum(dates).attr("d", area).attr("fill", POS).attr("opacity", 0.55).attr("clip-path", "url(#tone-above)");
        svg.append("path").datum(dates).attr("d", area).attr("fill", NEG).attr("opacity", 0.55).attr("clip-path", "url(#tone-below)");
        svg.append("path").datum(dates).attr("d", d3.line().defined((d, i) => t1[i] != null).x((d) => x(d)).y((d, i) => y(t1[i]))).attr("fill", "none").attr("stroke", INK).attr("stroke-width", 0.5).attr("opacity", 0.22);
        svg.append("path").datum(dates).attr("d", d3.line().defined((d, i) => t28[i] != null).x((d) => x(d)).y((d, i) => y(t28[i])).curve(d3.curveMonotoneX)).attr("fill", "none").attr("stroke", INK).attr("stroke-width", 1.2);
        svg.append("line").attr("x1", M.l).attr("x2", W - M.r).attr("y1", y(mean)).attr("y2", y(mean)).attr("stroke", MUTED).attr("stroke-dasharray", "3 4");
        capNote(el, `Decade mean <b>${sgn(mean)}</b> · ${swatch(POS, "kinder than usual")} ${swatch(NEG, "harsher than usual")} · faint line = daily, bold = 28-day mean.`);
        const dark = (tone.darkest ?? []).slice(0, 8).map((d, i) => ({ ...d, i, x: x(P(d.day)) }));
        const dg = svg.selectAll("g.dk").data(dark).join("g").attr("class", "dk");
        dg.append("circle").attr("cx", (d) => d.x).attr("cy", (d) => y(d.tone)).attr("r", 3.5).attr("fill", NEG).attr("stroke", GROUND)
          .on("mousemove", (e, d) => showTip(e, `<b>${fDay(P(d.day))}</b> · darkest day #${d.i + 1}<br>tone ${sgn(d.tone)} (${sgn(d.delta)} vs trailing month)<br>detailed below`))
          .on("mouseleave", hideTip);
        dg.append("text").attr("class", "annot alabel").attr("x", (d) => d.x).attr("y", (d) => y(d.tone) + 15).attr("text-anchor", "middle").attr("fill", NEG).text((d) => d.i + 1);
        const guide = svg.append("line").attr("y1", M.t).attr("y2", H - M.b).attr("stroke", INK).attr("stroke-opacity", 0.5).style("display", "none");
        hoverRect(svg, M, W, H, (e) => {
          const i = nearestIdx(dates, x.invert(d3.pointer(e)[0])); if (t1[i] == null) return;
          guide.style("display", null).attr("x1", x(dates[i])).attr("x2", x(dates[i]));
          showTip(e, `<b>${fDay(dates[i])}</b><br>tone <b style="color:${t1[i] < mean ? NEG : POS}">${sgn(t1[i])}</b> · 28-day ${sgn(t28[i])}<br>vs decade mean ${sgn(t1[i] - mean)}`);
        }, () => { guide.style("display", "none"); hideTip(); });
        // darkest-day cards
        const list = document.getElementById("darkest");
        list.innerHTML = `<h3>The ten darkest days</h3>` + (tone.darkest ?? []).map((d, i) => `
          <article class="day">
            <div class="day-head"><b>${i + 1} · ${fDay(P(d.day))}</b><span class="stamp" style="color:${NEG}">TONE ${sgn(d.tone)} · ${sgn(d.delta)} VS TRAILING MONTH</span><span class="stamp dim">${pct(d.vol)} OF WORLD NEWS${d.protests != null ? ` · ${d.protests} PROTEST EVENTS` : ""}</span></div>
            ${d.articles?.length ? `<ul>${d.articles.slice(0, 4).map((a) => `<li><a href="${a.url}" rel="noopener">${a.title}</a> <i>${a.domain}${a.country ? " · " + a.country : ""}</i></li>`).join("")}</ul>` : `<span class="stamp dim">HEADLINE SAMPLE PENDING (API CACHE)</span>`}
          </article>`).join("");
        const g20 = tone.g20;
        if (g20) {
          const rise = g20.report_only?.tone_rise, att = g20.signatures?.attention;
          document.getElementById("g20-note").innerHTML = `<b>An honest negative result.</b> The G20 summit in Bali (15 Nov 2022) ${att?.verdict === "PASS" ? `did lift attention (${num(att.ratio, 1)}× its trailing baseline)` : "did not lift attention above 1.5× baseline"}, but the world did <em>not</em> speak more warmly: the best tone day in the window was ${sgn(rise?.delta)} against the trailing mean${rise ? "" : " (not yet computed)"} — Ukraine and the missile strike in Poland ran through the same coverage. We report the number rather than the story we expected.`;
        }
      });

      sect("scatter", () => {
        const el = document.getElementById("scatter");
        const m = tone?.monthly; if (!m) { pending("scatter", "Pending API curves."); return; }
        const pts = m.months.map((mo, i) => ({ mo, d: PM(mo), vol: m.vol?.[i], tone: m.tone?.[i] })).filter((p) => p.vol != null && p.tone != null);
        if (pts.length < 6) { pending("scatter", "Pending API curves (monthly tone)."); return; }
        const M = { t: 16, r: 20, b: 36, l: 44 }, { svg, W, H } = mkSvg(el, 300);
        const x = d3.scaleLinear(d3.extent(pts, (p) => p.vol), [M.l, W - M.r]).nice();
        const y = d3.scaleLinear(d3.extent(pts, (p) => p.tone), [H - M.b, M.t]).nice();
        svg.append("g").attr("class", "axis").attr("transform", `translate(0,${H - M.b})`).call(d3.axisBottom(x).ticks(6).tickFormat((v) => v + "%"));
        svg.append("g").attr("class", "axis").attr("transform", `translate(${M.l},0)`).call(d3.axisLeft(y).ticks(5));
        svg.append("text").attr("class", "annot").attr("x", W - M.r).attr("y", H - 6).attr("text-anchor", "end").text("monthly share of world news →");
        svg.append("text").attr("class", "annot").attr("x", M.l + 4).attr("y", M.t + 10).text("↑ monthly tone");
        const eraOf = (d) => (pulse?.eras ?? []).findIndex((e) => P(e.start) <= d && d <= P(e.end));
        // fit line (least squares) for the annotation
        const mx = d3.mean(pts, (p) => p.vol), my = d3.mean(pts, (p) => p.tone);
        const b = d3.sum(pts, (p) => (p.vol - mx) * (p.tone - my)) / d3.sum(pts, (p) => (p.vol - mx) ** 2), a = my - b * mx;
        svg.append("line").attr("x1", x(x.domain()[0])).attr("x2", x(x.domain()[1])).attr("y1", y(a + b * x.domain()[0])).attr("y2", y(a + b * x.domain()[1])).attr("stroke", MUTED).attr("stroke-dasharray", "3 4");
        const r = d3.sum(pts, (p) => (p.vol - mx) * (p.tone - my)) / Math.sqrt(d3.sum(pts, (p) => (p.vol - mx) ** 2) * d3.sum(pts, (p) => (p.tone - my) ** 2));
        svg.append("text").attr("class", "annot").attr("x", W - M.r).attr("y", M.t + 10).attr("text-anchor", "end").text(`r = ${r.toFixed(2)} across ${pts.length} months`);
        svg.selectAll("circle").data(pts).join("circle").attr("cx", (p) => x(p.vol)).attr("cy", (p) => y(p.tone)).attr("r", 4.5)
          .attr("fill", (p) => ERA_COLORS[Math.max(0, eraOf(p.d)) % ERA_COLORS.length]).attr("opacity", 0.75).attr("stroke", GROUND).attr("stroke-width", 0.6)
          .on("mousemove", function (e, p) { d3.select(this).attr("opacity", 1).attr("r", 6.5); showTip(e, `<b>${fMon(p.d)}</b><br>share ${pct(p.vol)} · tone ${sgn(p.tone)}<br><span style="color:${ERA_COLORS[Math.max(0, eraOf(p.d)) % 5]}">${pulse?.eras?.[eraOf(p.d)]?.label ?? ""}</span>`); })
          .on("mouseleave", function () { d3.select(this).attr("opacity", 0.75).attr("r", 4.5); hideTip(); });
      });

      /* ---------- chapter 3: themes small multiples ---------- */
      sect("themes", () => {
        const el = document.getElementById("themes");
        const keys = (themes?.order ?? []).filter((k) => themes.themes[k]?.share?.some((v) => v != null));
        if (!keys.length) { pending("themes", "Pipeline still running — theme timelines are being fetched (one API call per theme, ~15 s apart)."); return; }
        const months = themes.months.map(PM);
        const panels = [];
        el.innerHTML = "";
        for (const k of keys) {
          const th = themes.themes[k];
          const wrap = document.createElement("div"); wrap.className = "panel"; wrap.dataset.theme = k;
          const nMo = th.share.filter((v) => v != null).length;
          const short = nMo < themes.months.length - 12;
          wrap.innerHTML = `<div class="panel-head"><b>${th.label}</b><span class="stamp ${short ? "warn" : "dim"}">${pct(100 * th.share_mean, 1)} MEAN · ${nMo} MO</span></div>`;
          el.appendChild(wrap);
          const M = { t: 6, r: 8, b: 18, l: 8 }, { svg, W, H } = mkSvg(wrap, 96);
          const x = d3.scaleTime(d3.extent(months), [M.l, W - M.r]);
          const vals = th.share.map((v) => (v == null ? null : 100 * v));
          const y = d3.scaleLinear([0, d3.max(vals) * 1.1 || 1], [H - M.b, M.t]);
          svg.append("g").attr("class", "axis tiny").attr("transform", `translate(0,${H - M.b})`).call(d3.axisBottom(x).ticks(d3.timeYear.every(3)).tickFormat(fYear).tickSize(3));
          svg.append("path").datum(months).attr("d", d3.area().defined((d, i) => vals[i] != null).x((d) => x(d)).y0(H - M.b).y1((d, i) => y(vals[i])).curve(d3.curveMonotoneX)).attr("fill", VIOLET).attr("opacity", 0.22);
          svg.append("path").datum(months).attr("d", d3.line().defined((d, i) => vals[i] != null).x((d) => x(d)).y((d, i) => y(vals[i])).curve(d3.curveMonotoneX)).attr("fill", "none").attr("stroke", VIOLET).attr("stroke-width", 1.4);
          const pk = d3.maxIndex(vals);
          svg.append("circle").attr("cx", x(months[pk])).attr("cy", y(vals[pk])).attr("r", 2.6).attr("fill", INK);
          svg.append("text").attr("class", "annot").attr("x", x(months[pk]) + (pk > months.length * 0.7 ? -5 : 5)).attr("text-anchor", pk > months.length * 0.7 ? "end" : "start").attr("y", Math.max(M.t + 9, y(vals[pk]) - 4)).text(`${fMon(months[pk])} · ${pct(vals[pk], 0)}`);
          const guide = svg.append("line").attr("y1", M.t).attr("y2", H - M.b).attr("stroke", INK).attr("stroke-opacity", 0.5).style("display", "none");
          panels.push({ k, x, guide, vals });
        }
        const moveAll = (e, i, k) => {
          panels.forEach((p) => p.guide.style("display", null).attr("x1", p.x(months[i])).attr("x2", p.x(months[i])));
          const rows = panels.map((p) => ({ k: p.k, v: p.vals[i] })).filter((r) => r.v != null).sort((a, b) => b.v - a.v).slice(0, 6);
          showTip(e, `<b>${fMon(months[i])}</b> · share of Indonesia coverage<br>${rows.map((r) => `<span style="color:${r.k === k ? VIOLET : INK}">${themes.themes[r.k].label} ${pct(r.v, 1)}</span>`).join("<br>")}`);
        };
        const leaveAll = () => { panels.forEach((p) => p.guide.style("display", "none")); hideTip(); };
        el.querySelectorAll(".panel").forEach((wrap) => {
          const k = wrap.dataset.theme, p = panels.find((q) => q.k === k);
          wrap.addEventListener("mousemove", (e) => { const rect = wrap.querySelector("svg").getBoundingClientRect(); const i = nearestIdx(months, p.x.invert(e.clientX - rect.left)); moveAll(e, i, k); });
          wrap.addEventListener("mouseleave", leaveAll);
        });
        // era ranking table
        const er = themes.era_rank ?? [];
        document.getElementById("era-rank").innerHTML = er.length ? `<h3>What each era was about</h3><div class="table-scroll"><table class="rank"><thead><tr><th>Era</th>${[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6].map((n) => `<th>#${n}</th>`).join("")}</tr></thead><tbody>${er.map((r) => `<tr><td class="era-name">${r.era}</td>${r.themes.map((t) => `<td><span>${themes.themes[t.key]?.label ?? t.key}</span><i>${pct(100 * t.share, 0)}</i></td>`).join("")}</tr>`).join("")}</tbody></table></div><p class="footnote">Share of Indonesia coverage that also matched the theme’s keywords (themes overlap; shares do not sum to 100%). Queries are listed in the methodology.</p>` : "";
      });

      /* ---------- chapter 4: who's talking ---------- */
      sect("sources heatmap", () => {
        const el = document.getElementById("sources-heat");
        if (!sources?.countries?.length) { pending("sources-heat", "Pipeline still running — the source-country timeline is not cached yet."); return; }
        const rows = sources.countries.filter((c) => c.name !== "Indonesia").slice(0, 14);
        const months = sources.months.map(PM);
        const M = { t: 26, r: 60, b: 28, l: 118 }, RH = 20, { svg, W, H } = mkSvg(el, M.t + rows.length * RH + M.b);
        const x = d3.scaleTime([months[0], d3.timeMonth.offset(months.at(-1), 1)], [M.l, W - M.r]);
        const cw = (W - M.l - M.r) / months.length;
        const vmax = d3.quantile(rows.flatMap((r) => r.values.filter((v) => v != null)), 0.98);
        const color = d3.scaleSequentialSqrt([0, vmax], d3.interpolateRgb(SURFACE, VIOLET)).clamp(true);
        svg.append("g").attr("class", "axis").attr("transform", `translate(0,${H - M.b})`).call(yearAxis(x));
        capNote(el, "Share of the country’s own monitored articles that mention Indonesia, monthly. Right-hand figure is the decade mean.");
        const g = svg.selectAll("g.row").data(rows).join("g").attr("class", "row").attr("transform", (d, i) => `translate(0,${M.t + i * RH})`);
        g.append("text").attr("class", "annot rowlab").attr("x", M.l - 8).attr("y", RH / 2 + 4).attr("text-anchor", "end").attr("fill", INK).text((d) => d.name);
        g.append("text").attr("class", "annot").attr("x", W - M.r + 8).attr("y", RH / 2 + 4).text((d) => pct(d.mean, 2));
        g.selectAll("rect").data((d) => d.values.map((v, i) => ({ v, i, name: d.name }))).join("rect")
          .attr("x", (c) => x(months[c.i])).attr("y", 1).attr("width", Math.max(1, cw - 0.5)).attr("height", RH - 2).attr("fill", (c) => (c.v == null ? GROUND : color(c.v)))
